        }
      ],
      "emotion": "reality_unveiled",
      "prompt_visual": "Subjective POV sequence showing Fuxi's new code vision: 1) A twisted swamp tree - now overlaid with cascading green text showing growth algorithms, nutrient flow data, age in rings/code. 2) The water surface - revealed as a molecular mesh network, hydrogen bonds visible as connecting lines, water chemistry formulas floating. 3) His own hand held up - beneath the skin, a web of blue biolelectric currents pulse, nervous system data streams visible, heartbeat represented as waveform. Each view maintains the primitive physical world but layers advanced visualization over it. The aesthetic blends organic nature with digital readout - like augmented reality from the future applied to the ancient world. Cut to medium shot of Fuxi, kneeling in water, staring at his hands in disbelief, his transformed left eye glowing as it processes this new reality.",
      "prompt_motion": "POV camera moves as Fuxi looks around. Each element he focuses on activates its code overlay. The data appears to render in real-time, like a system booting up. Text scrolls, diagrams animate, the whole world becomes a readable interface. His hand trembles as he examines it, watching his own bio-electricity flow. Finally, he speaks, voice cracking with overwhelmed emotion.",
      "transition_out": "j_cut",
      "transition_duration_s": 0,
      "transition_note": "J-cut: audio of the Entropy Units' mechanical arrival begins before the visual cuts. The ominous sound intrudes on Fuxi's moment of wonder, creating immediate threat tension. Audio: geometric descent hum begins 0.5s before visual transition.",
      "sfx_bgm": "Each code revelation has unique audio: trees have organic processing sounds, water has fluid data tones, bio-electricity crackles softly. Music is sparse, allowing wonder to breathe. Then the Entropy Units' approach sound begins - cold, mechanical, threatening.",
      "notes": "Defining visual language for the series: code vision. This is how Fuxi perceives reality now. The wonder must be palpable - then immediately threatened.",
      "location_ref": "vortex_edge"
    },
